Z||000015||Haze_Performance||06-29-2001||09:22 PM||||OK.... Heres my problem. He said the car has only 3 1/2 miles on it right? Unless he lived next to the dealer & the body shop that the kit was going to be installed.. Is he full of !@#*?... Lets say he trailered it.. Why would you trailer a new car that you were going to rip apart anyway? Also, not many cars arrive to the dealer with & are sold with 3 miles on it. Usually there is a few more by the time someone buys it. I for one bought a new car right off the showroom floor. (I watched them pull it off the truck and pull it in the room) It had 9 miles on it.  <P>Lets see. They drove the car from the factory assembly line to the holding yard. From the yard to a train or truck. From the train/truck to a holding yard. From there back on a truck to the dealers. Then all cars are driven around the dealer lots. From the rear holding the the display areas. Plus the car was never driven buy the owner or the shop? As was said before.. If the car hasn't ran in over 15 years, The motor and trans is garbage.<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank><BR>             <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/haze8588logo.gif">        </A>       <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/WS6_Fiero/photo.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>Pennock's Fiero Forum Members Photo Page</A><BR><A HREF="http://www.clubs.yahoo.com/clubs/ws6fiero" TARGET=_blank>WS6 Fiero Club</A><p>[This message has been edited by Haze_Performance (edited 06-30-2001).]||||reg||11
