Z||000017||Old Lar||06-29-2001||10:31 PM||||Haze  get a grip.  My new Fiero had 4 miles on it when I bought it.  Don't try to over analyze Hank's rolling chassie.  If you are not interested in it or can't afford it, don't bid on it.  I've seen it.  Hank has had it for many years.||||reg||1
Z||000018||Haze_Performance||06-30-2001||03:18 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Old Lar:<BR><B>Haze  get a grip.  My new Fiero had 4 miles on it when I bought it.  Don't try to over analyze Hank's rolling chassie.  If you are not interested in it or can't afford it, don't bid on it.  I've seen it.  Hank has had it for many years.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You had 4 miles after you bought it... How many miles did it have on it when you drove it home? All I'm saying is 3.5 miles on a over 15 year old car is a little to swallow. I also don't understand why a body shop had the car so long, and never reassembled it and sold it for a small fortune? Even now they wont even give you the rest of the parts with the sale of the car. It says you can buy them from them.<P><P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank><BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/haze8588logo.gif">       </A>       <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/WS6_Fiero/photo.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>Pennock's Fiero Forum Members Photo Page</A><BR><A HREF="http://www.clubs.yahoo.com/clubs/ws6fiero" TARGET=_blank>WS6 Fiero Club</A>||||reg||1
Z||000019||Old Lar||06-30-2001||07:39 AM||||The original body panels were sold off to fund the kit car conversion.  Hank had been assembling parts to rebuild the car, never making up his mind if he wanted to rebuild as stock or as a kit car. He has a collection of NOS parts which he'll sell of also. He had a ZR2 (one of the first).  He's just getting out of the Fiero collection of parts business, sold off the ZR2 and most of his miscellaneous parts, the big piece is his 3 mile rolling chassie.<P>This would be a good donor car for a kit car even though it's 15 years old and has no miles.  It can't be any worse than a 15 year old car with 100,000 miles on it, that may need lots of work to bring it back.<P>By the way, when I drove my car home from the dealer, (registered and licenced) I had 8 miles on the odometer.  It now has 85000 miles.<P>The original car was never licenced or driven on the road, but trailered around.||||reg||1
